<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Ben Oxley — geospatial systems engineer at Wayve, chartered engineer, builder and tinkerer">
  <article class="post">
    <h1>About Ben Oxley</h1>

    <p>
      Ben is an IC3 individual contributor on the Map and Route team at <a href="https://wayve.ai">Wayve</a>,
      building geospatial operations and analytics systems for Wayve's autonomous vehicle fleet.
      A certified cloud architect and a chartered mechanical and mechatronics engineer with over 12 years of
      experience, Ben thrives in implementing technically complex digital solutions with new and novel
      technologies across a wide range of domains.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ben enjoys understanding how things work and solving difficult problems integrating digital and physical
      systems. He excels in diving deep to understand how things work, with
      interest in everything from embedded electronics to geospatial data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ben also enjoys working with people to enable teams and companies to deliver to their potential. He
      is known for a collaborative and inclusive leadership style, enabling people to develop in a
      supportive and enthusiastic environment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside of work, Ben enjoys 3D printing geospatial data, building electronics and mountain biking (and
      sometimes a mixture of these).
    </p>

    <hr />

